\fs28\b POS V3 LAN Access Instructions\b0\par
\par
\fs22 Use this guide when one computer runs POS V3 and another computer connects to it from the same Wi-Fi or Ethernet network.\par
\par
\b 1. Start the server on the main POS computer\b0\par
\par
Open PowerShell and run:\par
\par
{\f1 cd "C:\\Users\\Portable\\Documents\\pos_v3_mauritius_products_left_billing_right (1)\\pos_v3_mauritius_professional_dashboard"\par
.\\start-lan-server.ps1\par}
\par
Keep the PowerShell window open while using POS V3.\par
\par
\b 2. Open POS V3 on the other computer\b0\par
\par
On the other computer, open a browser and go to:\par
\par
{\f1 http://192.168.100.3:8080\par}
\par
Both computers must be connected to the same Wi-Fi or Ethernet network.\par
\par
\b 3. Login\b0\par
\par
Default administrator login:\par
\par
{\f1 Username: admin\par
Password: admin123\par}
\par
Change the default password after setup.\par
\par
\b 4. If the other computer cannot connect\b0\par
\par
Windows Firewall may be blocking the connection. Open PowerShell as Administrator and run:\par
\par
{\f1 cd "C:\\Users\\Portable\\Documents\\pos_v3_mauritius_products_left_billing_right (1)\\pos_v3_mauritius_professional_dashboard"\par
.\\start-lan-server.ps1 -OpenFirewall\par}
\par
If Windows shows this Wi-Fi or Ethernet network as Public, either change the network profile to Private in Windows Settings, or use this on a trusted network only:\par
\par
{\f1 .\\start-lan-server.ps1 -OpenFirewall -AllowPublicNetwork\par}
\par
You can also double-click open-pos-firewall-admin.bat and approve the Windows administrator prompt.\par
\par
Then try again from the other computer:\par
\par
{\f1 http://192.168.100.3:8080\par}
\par
\b 5. If port 8080 is already used\b0\par
\par
Start POS V3 on another port:\par
\par
{\f1 .\\start-lan-server.ps1 -Port 8090\par}
\par
Then connect from the other computer with:\par
\par
{\f1 http://192.168.100.3:8090\par}
\par
\b 6. Use only the IP address\b0\par
\par
To open POS V3 on the other computer with only the IP address, run POS V3 on port 80.\par
\par
On the main POS computer, double-click:\par
\par
{\f1 start-ip-only-server-admin.bat\par}
\par
Approve the Windows administrator prompt. Then open this on the other computer:\par
\par
{\f1 http://192.168.100.3\par}
\par
\b Security note\b0\par
\par
Only use this on a trusted local network. Do not expose this POS system directly to the public internet.\par
}
